    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d908">

                <pb facs="0912" n="654" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg654"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/2061</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Germany</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >Gerard</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2034]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-12-14">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">December 14, 1915</hi>.</date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received December 30</hi>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s
                    telegraphic instructions of October 28, 1915, serial telegram No. 2350, and to
                    my telegram No. 3172 of December 2, 1915,<anchor n="1" xml:id="d908-f1"/>
                    regarding certain inquiries in connection with the possible importation of
                    conditional contraband into Germany, especially as to what extent the German
                    civil authorities have been superseded by the German military authorities, I
                    have the honor to transmit herewith enclosed a copy and a translation of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">note verbale</hi> No. IIIa 22501 from the German Foreign
                    Office, which has been to-day received in reply to my representations on the
                    subject.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">James W. Gerard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d908-a1.xml" xpointer="d908-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
